WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.667
Moscow is

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.201
pointing the

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.503
finger at Washington, baselessly

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.071
claiming the US directed

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.007
Ukraine to carry out this alleged drone

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.842
strike on the Kremlin.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.977
Kiev has also denied involvement

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.445
and so is the US.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.847
Here's what a top White House

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.882
official told CNN earlier today

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.652
about this latest assertion from Russia.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.721
There's a word that comes to mind

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.023
that I'm obviously not.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.125
Not appropriate to use on national TV.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.059
I would just tell you, Mr.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.093
Press. Gov's lying.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.862
I mean, obviously it's a ludicrous claim.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.429
The United States

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.296
had nothing to do with it.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.998
We don't even know exactly what happened

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.233
here, Caitlin.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:33.833
But I can assure you

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.735
the United States had had no role in it

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.137
whatsoever.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.905
Strong words from the administration

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:39.839
there for Russia, though

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.608
it may not matter who did this.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.043
Vladimir Putin's forces

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.144
have already used it

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.046
as a pretext for retaliation,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.580
unleashing a fierce

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.482
wave of attacks on Kiev and other

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.017
Ukrainian cities.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.218
Drones that fired on

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.120
Odessa even had messages on them.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.721
Take a look.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.423
This reads for Moscow

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.791
and for the Kremlin.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:58.425
That's according

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.993
to the Ukrainian military.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.195
CNN's Nick Paton Walsh is in Ukraine.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.463
And Nick Cave is saying it's

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.398
worse attacks in months.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.499
We know that an oil

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.635
refinery was hit in Russia.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.437
It seems that both sides

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.640
are really escalating here.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.142
Yeah, certainly.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.443
I mean, what

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.710
would be saying over the past three

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.678
or four days here in

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.081
Ukraine is an increased tempo

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.816
of Russian strikes.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.250
Often hitting civilian areas

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.585
as far as we can see.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.020
Last night,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.255
Kiev saying that the last three nights

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:29.956
are the worst

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.825
since the year began last night.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.194
Many drones taken down out of the sky,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.829
not actually hitting targets

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.729
in the capital.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.498
Similar story over Odessa

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.233
as well in the south of the country.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.302
So compared to previous nights

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.803
where we've seen

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.905
cities across the country

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.740
with civilian targets hit

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.709
and the loss of life last night,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.810
not the worst,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.578
but yesterday

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:52.479
and had some

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.180
city recently liberated

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:54.747
from Russian

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.283
occupiers, 24 people lost their lives

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.319
in the shelling of a shopping center

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.587
and a railway station.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.921
Clear civilian areas

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.923
being hit by repeated shelling.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.492
Now, this is really,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.793
I think, the escalation

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.161
Ukrainians are worried about

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.662
when Russian in that statement

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.264
where they presented no evidence

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:11.798
but said there'd

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.299
been an attempted assassination

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.634
on the president said

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.736
that they reserve the right to retaliate

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.537
even today.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:18.972
Peskov, the

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.740
Kremlin spokesperson, didn't go into what

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.142
that would necessarily mean.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.243
He said that Vladimir Putin

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.711
was calm and considered

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.945
after this incident

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:26.646
and even referred

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.413
to how the damage

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.582
to the Kremlin roof was to bits of copper

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.050
that probably would get fixed

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.085
later on today.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.287
So a lot of concern here about what

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.822
this may be teeing up

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.590
in terms of Russian response,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.392
but Ukraine's counteroffensive

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.894
likely imminent.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.761
All right, Nick Paton

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.630
Walsh with the latest from Ukraine.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.465
Thanks so much for that update. And Jim.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.699
Now we've got those details.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.434
You guys have some analysis over here.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.903
Let's try to figure out how credible

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.304
these claims are.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.372
Joining me now,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.507
we have someone who knows a thing or two

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.177
about this, retired Brigadier General.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.411
Steve Anderson, first

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:58.811
to get to

00:02:58.811 --> 00:02:59.345
this claim

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.880
that this was a Ukrainian strike

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.948
on the Kremlin.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:02.916
Let's look at the sites

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.485
of Ukrainian strikes on Russian territory

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.119
so far.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.087
Here's the here's the border of Ukraine.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.923
They've been able to strike Belgorod

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.125
just a couple dozen miles away

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:12.992
from Ukraine.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.060
Down in Crimea,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.928
certainly accessible

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.429
from Ukrainian territory.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.730
Also in Krasnodar.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.068
This one would be 300 miles into the draw

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:22.468
the straight line,

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.337
but three, two miles in a straight line

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.039
into Ukrainian territory.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:26.839
How credible is that?

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.775
It is not credible, Jim.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:29.442
It really

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.443
there's no way,

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.311
I think, that

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.780
the the Ukrainian drones

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.914
would be able to penetrate

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.382
some of the most sophisticated air

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.218
defenses in the world.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.953
500 miles or so from Kiev,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.154
all the way to Moscow.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.322
It's just not going to happen.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.690
I mean, that's just not a scenario

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.358
that's really reasonable.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.259
And I imagine those

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.093
those air defenses

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.028
would be particularly intent

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.763
on protecting this area. Absolutely.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.365
They'd be focused on Moscow.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.566
And they have, again,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.335
incredibly efficient

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.804
and effective air defenses.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.638
The last time

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.739
that any kind of penetration

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.641
occurred was in 1987, 35

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.209
years ago, with a little Piper Cub

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.577
that was able to fly into Red Square.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.346
But since then, it's been locked down

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.847
pretty tight and certainly

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:08.915
with a war going on.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.950
They're going to be incredibly effective.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.986
Okay.
Let's look at the start of the strikes.

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.121
This is where Russia has struck

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.489
since this

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.324
this attack on the Kremlin, calling them,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.193
in effect, retaliatory strikes.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.261
They've been hitting hard,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.161
certainly a frequent target,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.030
of course, close to Russian territory

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.832
down here in Herston, recently

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.467
taken back from Russia

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.701
by Ukrainian forces.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.503
And, of course, the capital, Kiev.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.138
A lot of talk about targeting

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:32.805
the Ukrainian

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.774
president, Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.676
Are these attempts to do that?

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:37.844
There might very well, Jim.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.811
I mean, that would be something

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.413
I'd be very worried about.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.248
You know, the false flag,

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.217
I think that we saw yesterday

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.286
of attack on the Kremlin

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.121
maybe sets the stage for hey, look,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.222
they went after me.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.356
Vladimir Putin saying now

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.958
it's my turn to go after Zelensky.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.027
So I would definitely if I was

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.194
on his security detail,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.530
zelensky's security, I'd

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.399
definitely step up my game.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.933
But, you know, this is terrorizing

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:01.467
the people.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.735
Terrorizing the president is something

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:03.336
that that's

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:03.736
that's how

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.804
they've been playing this whole thing.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.005
And that's our only real play.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.807
You mention false flag

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.742
that would be a Russian attack

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.311
claiming to be a Ukrainian attack.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:11.911
By the way,

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.446
Russia attempted several of these.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.347
What I was in Ukraine

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.782
at the start of the invasion, which U.S.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.483
intelligence exposed and hey,

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.685
these are not Ukrainian attacks.

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:19.552
It's a Russian plan,

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:20.887
a propaganda plan here.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.688
We had a remarkable

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:24.257
charge made by a former Russian lawmaker

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.224
who spoke to my colleague,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.359
Matthew Chance

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.894
about another possibility

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.629
for the origin of this attack.

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:30.229
Have a listen.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.230
And I want to get your reaction.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.001
Are any of these partizans

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.903
supported by

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.538
the Ukrainian special services,

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:39.138
for instance,

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.273
because Ukraine says it's

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.642
got nothing to do with this attack.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.544
Do you believe that claim?

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:45.211
Well, look,

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.280
Ukrainians, it has nothing to do with us

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:52.652
because it's all organized by Russians.

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:53.753
He's saying

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:55.822
this could be a Russian attack

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.123
on Russia partizans

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.691
those who oppose the leadership

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.926
of vladimir putin.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:00.426
Credible.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.428
It's a credible scenario,

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.530
probably not likely, but it's possible.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.499
I mean, these are large drones.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.200
They could have to

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.201
they'd have to hide them

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.335
in a shipping container

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:10.503
or a truck of some sort,

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.138
somehow get it close to Moscow,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.940
perhaps pull them out, launch them.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.540
I mean, those kind

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.775
of things could happen.

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:17.176
But I think it's pretty unlikely.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.278
I think it's really much a false flag

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.680
operation that has occurred.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.949
And and we're seeing the reaction

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:23.282
to that.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.751
Well, part of that false flag operation

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:26.486
would be the follow on.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.687
This is a message

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.088
for the Kremlin

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.223
on one of the Russian drone

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.791
drones fired at Ukraine

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.292
in the wake of all this.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:34.060
Retired General Steve

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:34.961
Anderson, thanks so much.

